      {
        "description": "Species interaction matrices per replicate (4 stages ∗ 3 replicates = 12 interaction matrices) based on the observed species. Rare species (≤1 individual in total) were excluded from the matrix to exclude ecological irrelevant species interactions.\nSheets show one replicate of state of mangrove forest: climax, degrading (D), colonizing (Col), bare (B) and replicate ID (1-3) \nRows and columns indicate consumer*resource species: 0= not eaten; 1= resource eaten by consumer.\nUsed for figs 2,3 and 4.",
